1
00:00:04,816 --> 00:00:07,066
Commerce, and Industry and Supply, merge into one Ministry of Commerce and Industry.

2
00:00:07,066 --> 00:00:09,416
Works, Mines and Power breaks up: Works, Housing and Supply; Production; and river valley schemes go to Planning.

3
00:00:10,367 --> 00:00:12,517
The Ministry of States, which integrated the princely states, joins Home Affairs.

4
00:00:12,517 --> 00:00:15,067
Railways becomes a ministry of its own; Transport takes in Communications.

5
00:00:15,611 --> 00:00:17,311
The Allocation of Business Rules, 1961 begin (14 January 1961). From here a ministry's size is its count of subjects in the Second Schedule; before this, ministries come from the cabinet lists and sizes are worked back from 1961.

6
00:00:17,311 --> 00:00:19,861
Scientific Research and Cultural Affairs separates from Education.

7
00:00:20,486 --> 00:00:22,836
Steel, Mines and Fuel divides into Mines and Fuel, and Steel and Heavy Industries.

8
00:00:23,581 --> 00:00:25,931
Commerce and Industry divides: International Trade and Industry become ministries of their own.

9
00:00:27,002 --> 00:00:29,252
Labour and Employment, and Rehabilitation, merge into one ministry.

10
00:00:32,743 --> 00:00:34,693
The Department of Space is created.

11
00:00:39,116 --> 00:00:41,666
A Department of Environment is carved out of Science and Technology.

12
00:00:44,190 --> 00:00:45,890
The Second Schedule is printed afresh (S.O. 696(E), 25 September 1985): its subjects reworded and renumbered, with the year's reorganisation.

13
00:00:45,890 --> 00:00:48,240
In the 1985 re-issue, Irrigation and Power divides into Water Resources and Energy.

14
00:00:48,841 --> 00:00:51,191
Transport divides into Surface Transport and Civil Aviation.

15
00:00:53,657 --> 00:00:56,007
Energy divides into Power and Non-Conventional Energy Sources, and Coal.

16
00:00:59,885 --> 00:01:01,835
A Ministry of Tribal Affairs is created.

17
00:01:01,835 --> 00:01:04,185
Planning and Programme Implementation divides: Statistics and Programme Implementation, and Planning.

18
00:01:05,218 --> 00:01:07,168
A Department of Development of North Eastern Region is created.

19
00:01:07,268 --> 00:01:09,518
Communications and Information Technology merge into one ministry.

20
00:01:10,591 --> 00:01:12,291
Both schedules are printed afresh (S.O. 17(E), 6 January 2004): the units' subjects reworded and renumbered.

21
00:01:12,391 --> 00:01:14,641
Coal and Mines merge into one ministry.

22
00:01:15,211 --> 00:01:17,361
The Ministry of Disinvestment is folded into Finance.

23
00:01:17,721 --> 00:01:20,071
Eleven months later, Coal and Mines part again.

24
00:01:20,787 --> 00:01:23,337
Minority Affairs is carved out of Social Justice.

25
00:01:23,337 --> 00:01:25,887
Women and Child Development becomes a ministry of its own, out of HRD.

26
00:01:29,957 --> 00:01:32,307
Skills and Sports, joined in July, divide in December.

27
00:01:32,307 --> 00:01:34,857
AYUSH buds off Health and Family Welfare.

28
00:01:35,070 --> 00:01:37,120
The Planning Commission is abolished…

29
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:39,070
…and NITI Aayog is created in its place.

30
00:01:39,638 --> 00:01:41,788
Overseas Indian Affairs folds into External Affairs.

31
00:01:42,061 --> 00:01:44,411
Communications and IT divide: Electronics & IT becomes a ministry.

32
00:01:46,021 --> 00:01:48,571
Fisheries, Animal Husbandry and Dairying leaves Agriculture.

33
00:01:48,571 --> 00:01:50,721
Drinking Water and Sanitation folds into Water Resources…

34
00:01:50,721 --> 00:01:52,621
…which is renamed the Ministry of Jal Shakti.

35
00:01:53,258 --> 00:01:55,158
Human Resource Development is renamed Education.

36
00:01:55,601 --> 00:01:58,151
A new Ministry of Cooperation is carved out of Agriculture.
